<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1. </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the theory of projective curves, one of the most important problem is to understand complete linear series on a curve and the maps to projective spaces defined by them. Concerning this problem, one can have a very detailed picture if either the curve in question has a very small genus, or the degree of the line bundle in question is large enough (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx1" title="" class="ltx_ref">C</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx2" title="" class="ltx_ref">E</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx5" title="" class="ltx_ref">F</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx6" title="" class="ltx_ref">G</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx7" title="" class="ltx_ref">GL1</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx8" title="" class="ltx_ref">GL2</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx9" title="" class="ltx_ref">L</a>]</cite>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx10" title="" class="ltx_ref">M</a>]</cite>, etc). On the other hand, it is impossible to say much about arbitrary cases. The main goal of this paper is to study the problem for line bundles on a hyperelliptic curve from various natural viewpoints.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a hyperelliptic curve of arithmetic genus <math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. a projective integral (possibly singular) curve such that <math id="S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(C,\mathcal{O}_{C})\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(C,\mathcal{O}_{C})\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and there is a degree two map <math id="S1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is well-known that <math id="S1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely determined, up to automorphisms of <math id="S1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="S1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=f^{*}\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=f^{*}\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique line bundle on <math id="S1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> defining a <math id="S1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{1}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{1}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also <math id="S1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{C}=A^{g-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{C}=A^{g-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="S1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Gorenstein (c.f. Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2. The Hyperelliptic Factorization ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>). One can define a natural factorization of line bundles on <math id="S1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="S1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a line bundle on <math id="S1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider the integer <math id="S1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by</p>
<table id="S1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathcal{L}}:=\mbox{max}~\{t\in{\mathbb{Z}}~|~H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-t})\neq 0\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext>max</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathcal{L}}:=\mbox{max}~\{t\in{\mathbb{Z}}~|~H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-t})\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="S1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> can be factorized as <math id="S1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=A^{m_{\mathcal{L}}}\otimes B_{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=A^{m_{\mathcal{L}}}\otimes B_{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\mathcal{L}}:=\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-m_{\mathcal{L}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\mathcal{L}}:=\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-m_{\mathcal{L}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\mathcal{L}}=\mbox{deg}(B_{\mathcal{L}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>deg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\mathcal{L}}=\mbox{deg}(B_{\mathcal{L}})</annotation></semantics></math>. The pair <math id="S1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{\mathcal{L}},b_{\mathcal{L}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{\mathcal{L}},b_{\mathcal{L}})</annotation></semantics></math> will be called <span id="S1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the factorization type of</span> <math id="S1.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this paper, we are intended to investigate the relation between the algebraic and geometric properties of <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and the factorization type of <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. It will turn out that the pair <math id="S1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{\mathcal{L}},b_{\mathcal{L}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{\mathcal{L}},b_{\mathcal{L}})</annotation></semantics></math> gives a precise answer for many natural questions about <math id="S1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In Section 2 we study a geometric meaning of the above factorization. Let <math id="S1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> be the smooth rational ruled surface <math id="S1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b_{\mathcal{L}}-g-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b_{\mathcal{L}}-g-1))</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math> denote respectively the minimal section of <math id="S1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and a fiber of the projection morphism <math id="S1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2. The Hyperelliptic Factorization ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> shows that <math id="S1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is embedded in <math id="S1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> as a divisor linearly equivalent to <math id="S1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2C_{0}+(2g+2-b_{\mathcal{L}})\mathfrak{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2C_{0}+(2g+2-b_{\mathcal{L}})\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <math id="S1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔣</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\mathcal{L}}=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\mathcal{L}}=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore we can regard <math id="S1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> as the restriction of the line bundle <math id="S1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m_{\mathcal{L}}\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m_{\mathcal{L}}\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the complete linear series on <math id="S1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> are very well understood, this observation enables us to study the line bundle <math id="S1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> from several viewpoints.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In Section 3 we solve the problem of the Riemann-Roch, i.e. the computation of the dimension of the <math id="S1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-vector spaces <math id="S1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(C,\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(C,\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math>, and of the base point freeness and the very ampleness of <math id="S1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Base Point Freeness And Very Ampleness ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> shows how these properties of <math id="S1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> are precisely determined by the factorization type <math id="S1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{\mathcal{L}},b_{\mathcal{L}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{\mathcal{L}},b_{\mathcal{L}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Also this result gives a complete list of base point free ample line bundles and very ample line bundles on <math id="S1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Then in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 3.4. ‣ 3. Base Point Freeness And Very Ampleness ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, we provide a rounded picture of the map <math id="S1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is base point free but not very ample. As a byproduct, we obtain the classification of birationally very ample line bundles on <math id="S1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Through Section 4 <math id="S1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> Section 6, we study the linearly normal embedding of <math id="S1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a very ample line bundle on <math id="S1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and with the factorization type <math id="S1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider the linearly normal curve</p>
<table id="S1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}={\mathbb{P}}^{r},~r=d-g," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}={\mathbb{P}}^{r},~r=d-g,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">embedded by <math id="S1.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{L}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{L}|</annotation></semantics></math>. A natural approach to study <math id="S1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is to investigate the Hartshorne-Rao module, the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity, and the graded Betti numbers of the minimal free resolution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">In Section 4 we consider the case where <math id="S1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2g+1+p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2g+1+p</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is projectively normal and so <math id="S1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-regular. In Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4. Minimal Free Resolution I - High Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we obtain all the graded Betti numbers of <math id="S1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. They depend only on <math id="S1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, and so <math id="S1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math> has no effect on the form of the minimal free resolution. As a corollary, <math id="S1.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies Green-Lazarsfeld’s property <math id="S1.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> while it fails to satisfy property <math id="S1.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, which was first proved in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx8" title="" class="ltx_ref">GL2</a>]</cite> when <math id="S1.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth. Recall that a line bundle <math id="S1.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S1.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2g+1+p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2g+1+p</annotation></semantics></math> on a smooth projective curve <math id="S1.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> of genus <math id="S1.p7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> fails to satisfy property <math id="S1.p7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if either <math id="S1.p7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(X,L\otimes\omega_{X}^{-1})\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>X</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(X,L\otimes\omega_{X}^{-1})\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="S1.p7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(X,L)^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(X,L)^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a <math id="S1.p7.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+3)</annotation></semantics></math>-secant <math id="S1.p7.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-plane or <math id="S1.p7.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> is hyperelliptic (<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx8" title="" class="ltx_ref">GL2</a>, Theorem 2]</cite>). Thus it is an interesting problem to find a finite subscheme of <math id="S1.p7.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> which obstructs property <math id="S1.p7.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S1.p7.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math>. In Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1. ‣ 6. Minimal Free Resolution III - Geometric Meaning ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a>, we show that the failure of property <math id="S1.p7.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> comes from a very special geometric property of <math id="S1.p7.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S1.p7.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a <math id="S1.p7.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+3)</annotation></semantics></math>-secant <math id="S1.p7.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-plane if and only if <math id="S1.p7.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq g-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq g-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus for <math id="S1.p7.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq g-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq g-2</annotation></semantics></math>, it is necessary to find a new geometric obstruction of property <math id="S1.p7.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Along this line, we show that the unique effective divisor <math id="S1.p7.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma:=C\cap C_{0}\in|B_{\mathcal{L}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma:=C\cap C_{0}\in|B_{\mathcal{L}}|</annotation></semantics></math> causes the failure of property <math id="S1.p7.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> since</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S1.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">a.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the rational normal curve <math id="S1.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">b.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\Gamma\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\Gamma\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(p+g-m)+(g+1-m)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(p+g-m)+(g+1-m)\}</annotation></semantics></math>-secant <math id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+g-m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+g-m)</annotation></semantics></math>-plane to <math id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S1.I1.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+1-m\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+1-m\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">For example, suppose that <math id="S1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2g+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)=(g-2,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)=(g-2,5)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the corresponding linearly normal curve <math id="S1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> has no tri-secant line while it admits a <math id="S1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>-secant <math id="S1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-plane. Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 6.1. ‣ 6. Minimal Free Resolution III - Geometric Meaning ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.1</span></a> shows that the <math id="S1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>-secant <math id="S1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-plane <math id="S1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\Gamma\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\Gamma\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> provides a geometric reason why the homogeneous ideal of <math id="S1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> cannot be generated by quadrics. Therefore the factorization of <math id="S1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is deeply related to the minimal free resolution of <math id="S1.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. This result enables us to have a coherent comprehension that the failure of property <math id="S1.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S1.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,L)</annotation></semantics></math> is always caused by the existence of an appropriate multi-secant linear space to <math id="S1.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(X,L)^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(X,L)^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">In Section 5 we consider the case where <math id="S1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq 2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq 2g</annotation></semantics></math>. Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5. Minimal Free Resolution II - Low Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> shows that many important cohomological and homological properties of <math id="S1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> are governed by the factorization type of <math id="S1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. More precisely, the Hartshorne-Rao module and the minimal free resolution are precisely determined by <math id="S1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, the Betti diagrams of two line bundles with the same factorization type are equal to each other. This enables us to understand how many distinct Betti diagrams occur at all (Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 6.3. ‣ 6. Minimal Free Resolution III - Geometric Meaning ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a> and Remark <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem4" title="Remark 6.4. ‣ 6. Minimal Free Resolution III - Geometric Meaning ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.4</span></a>)</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, in Section 7 we present some examples that illustrate the results proven in Section 5 and Section 6.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2. </span>The Hyperelliptic Factorization</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this section, <math id="S2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a hyperelliptic curve of arithmetic genus <math id="S2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> admits a degree two map <math id="S2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=f^{*}\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=f^{*}\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. We begin with investigating some properties of <math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> related to <math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, which belong to folklore for smooth case.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique line bundle on <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> defining <math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{1}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{1}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{C}=A^{g-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{C}=A^{g-1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and hence </span><math id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is locally Gorenstein.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">(1) Let <math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa:\widetilde{C}\rightarrow C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa:\widetilde{C}\rightarrow C</annotation></semantics></math> be the normalization of <math id="S2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> be the genus of <math id="S2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\circ\kappa:\widetilde{C}\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\circ\kappa:\widetilde{C}\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a degree two morphism. Let <math id="S2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> be a line bundle on <math id="S2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="S2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{deg}(A^{\prime})=h^{0}(C,A^{\prime})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>deg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{deg}(A^{\prime})=h^{0}(C,A^{\prime})=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the morphism defined by <math id="S2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the following commutative diagram:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{CD}\widetilde{C}&amp;\quad\quad\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\kappa}}{{\rightarrow}}\quad&amp;C\\
&amp;h\circ\kappa\searrow\quad&amp;\downarrow h\\
&amp;&amp;{\mathbb{P}}^{1}\end{CD}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mrow><mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>κ</mi></mover><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi>C</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>↘</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{CD}\widetilde{C}&amp;\quad\quad\stackrel{{\scriptstyle\kappa}}{{\rightarrow}}\quad&amp;C\\
&amp;h\circ\kappa\searrow\quad&amp;\downarrow h\\
&amp;&amp;{\mathbb{P}}^{1}\end{CD}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">To verify that <math id="S2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=A^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=A^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to show that <math id="S2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\circ\kappa=f\circ\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\circ\kappa=f\circ\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth hyperelliptic curve and hence <math id="S2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\circ\kappa=f\circ\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\circ\kappa=f\circ\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=1</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mbox{Sing}(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Sing</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mbox{Sing}(C)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h\circ\kappa)^{*}\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(1)=(\kappa^{*}\mathcal{I}_{x/C})^{-1}=(f\circ\kappa)^{*}\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(1)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h\circ\kappa)^{*}\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(1)=(\kappa^{*}\mathcal{I}_{x/C})^{-1}=(f\circ\kappa)^{*}\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">and hence <math id="S2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\circ\kappa=f\circ\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\circ\kappa=f\circ\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S2.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S2.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be the degree two embedding. Then degree two maps <math id="S2.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is parameterized by <math id="S2.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{2}\setminus\widetilde{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∖</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{2}\setminus\widetilde{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now let <math id="S2.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mbox{Sing}(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext>Sing</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mbox{Sing}(C)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S2.p3.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa^{*}\mathcal{I}_{x/C})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa^{*}\mathcal{I}_{x/C})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p3.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa^{*}\mathcal{I}_{y/C})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa^{*}\mathcal{I}_{y/C})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> determines distinct two lines which meet at a point <math id="S2.p3.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in{\mathbb{P}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in{\mathbb{P}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="S2.p3.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\circ\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\circ\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> should be the linear projection of <math id="S2.p3.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{C}\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{C}\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S2.p3.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, it is uniquely determined by <math id="S2.p3.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">(2) Since <math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(C,A^{g-1})\geq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(C,A^{g-1})\geq g</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}(C,A^{g-1})=h^{0}(\omega_{C}\otimes A^{-g+1})&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}(C,A^{g-1})=h^{0}(\omega_{C}\otimes A^{-g+1})&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This shows that <math id="S2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{C}\otimes A^{-g+1}=\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{C}\otimes A^{-g+1}=\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> since the degree of the quasi-invertible sheaf <math id="S2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{C}\otimes A^{-g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{C}\otimes A^{-g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is zero. Therefore <math id="S2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{C}=A^{g-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{C}=A^{g-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is locally Gorenstein.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Now we introduce to a natural factorization of line bundles on <math id="S2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="S2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. It will turn out through the remaining sections that all the algebraic and geometric properties of complete linear series on <math id="S2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> are explicitly determined by the type of this factorization.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.2</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a line bundle on <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(1) The integer <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathcal{L}}:=\mbox{max}~\{t\in{\mathbb{Z}}~|~H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-t})\neq 0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext>max</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0.330em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathcal{L}}:=\mbox{max}~\{t\in{\mathbb{Z}}~|~H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-t})\neq 0\}</annotation></semantics></math> is called the multiplicity of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{\mathcal{L}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{\mathcal{L}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then we say that <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is normalized.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">(2) The line bundle <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\mathcal{L}}:=\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-m_{\mathcal{L}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\mathcal{L}}:=\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-m_{\mathcal{L}}}</annotation></semantics></math>
is called the normalized part of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">(3) The integer <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\mathcal{L}}:=\mbox{deg}(\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-m_{\mathcal{L}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mtext>deg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\mathcal{L}}:=\mbox{deg}(\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-m_{\mathcal{L}}})</annotation></semantics></math>
is called the normalized degree of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">(4) <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=A^{m_{\mathcal{L}}}\otimes B_{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=A^{m_{\mathcal{L}}}\otimes B_{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be the hyperelliptic factorization of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">(5) We say that <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{\mathcal{L}},b_{\mathcal{L}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{\mathcal{L}},b_{\mathcal{L}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the factorization type of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The hyperelliptic factorization of <math id="S2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is unique in the sense that if <math id="S2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=A^{m}\otimes B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=A^{m}\otimes B</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is normalized, then <math id="S2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=m_{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=m_{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=B_{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=B_{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also the normalized degree of <math id="S2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> should satisfy <math id="S2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq b_{\mathcal{L}}\leq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq b_{\mathcal{L}}\leq g+1</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, for any integer <math id="S2.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq b\leq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq b\leq g+1</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a normalized line bundle of degree <math id="S2.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. More precisely, consider smooth points <math id="S2.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> such that no two of the <math id="S2.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>’s are conjugate under the hyperelliptic involution. Then <math id="S2.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{C}(P_{1}+\cdots+P_{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{C}(P_{1}+\cdots+P_{b})</annotation></semantics></math> is a normalized line bundle of degree <math id="S2.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">A crucial geometric meaning of this factorization is provided by</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2.3</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mbox{Pic}C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Pic</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mbox{Pic}C</annotation></semantics></math> be a normalized line bundle of degree <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> be the smooth rational ruled surface <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b-g-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b-g-1))</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there is an embedding of <math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset S</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the following three conditions:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔣</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">; and</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is linearly equivalent to </span><math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2C_{0}+(2g+2-b)\mathfrak{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2C_{0}+(2g+2-b)\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as a divisor of </span><math id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.I1.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Here </span><math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> denote respectively the minimal section of </span><math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and a fiber of the projection map </span><math id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.Thmtheorem3.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the line bundle <math id="S2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}:=A^{g+2}\otimes B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}:=A^{g+2}\otimes B</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2g+4+b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2g+4+b</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> a non-special very ample line bundle, and that the linearly normal curve</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}={\mathbb{P}}^{r},\quad r=g+b+4," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}={\mathbb{P}}^{r},\quad r=g+b+4,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">embedded by the complete linear series <math id="S2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{L}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{L}|</annotation></semantics></math> is cut out by quadrics (cf. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx5" title="" class="ltx_ref">F</a>]</cite>). In particular, <math id="S2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> does not admit a tri-secant line.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first construct a smooth rational normal surface scroll <math id="S2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> which contains <math id="S2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. This can be done by Eisenbud-Koh-Stillman’s method in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx3" title="" class="ltx_ref">EKS</a>]</cite>. One can also find the details in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx2" title="" class="ltx_ref">E</a>, Chapter VI]</cite>. Consider the multiplication map</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:H^{0}(C,A)\otimes H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-1})\rightarrow H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:H^{0}(C,A)\otimes H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-1})\rightarrow H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">If we choose bases <math id="S2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e_{1},e_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e_{1},e_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{f_{1},\cdots,f_{r-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{f_{1},\cdots,f_{r-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(C,A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(C,A)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively, then the <math id="S2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times(r-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times(r-1)</annotation></semantics></math> matrix</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(A,\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-1}):=(\mu(e_{i}\otimes f_{j}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(A,\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-1}):=(\mu(e_{i}\otimes f_{j}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">can be regarded as a matrix of linear forms on <math id="S2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is a <math id="S2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-generic matrix and hence its <math id="S2.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> minors define a rational normal surface scroll <math id="S2.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> which contains <math id="S2.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Also <math id="S2.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth since <math id="S2.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is surjective. Geometrically, <math id="S2.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> can be defined as</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S=\bigcup_{y\in{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}&lt;f^{-1}(y)&gt;\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.111em">&lt;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\bigcup_{y\in{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}&lt;f^{-1}(y)&gt;\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S2.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the degree two map.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we will determine the numerical type of <math id="S2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and the divisor class of <math id="S2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth rational ruled surface, there is an integer <math id="S2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S={\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-e))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S={\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-e)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math> be respectively the minimal section of <math id="S2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and a fiber of the projection map <math id="S2.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S2.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\equiv kC_{0}+\ell\mathfrak{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\equiv kC_{0}+\ell\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S2.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.p10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is not a smooth rational curve, <math id="S2.p10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. On the other hand, the rulings of <math id="S2.p10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="S2.p10.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-secant lines to <math id="S2.p10.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. So <math id="S2.p10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> cannot be cut out by quadrics if <math id="S2.p10.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>. In conclusion, <math id="S2.p10.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math> and so the restriction of <math id="S2.p10.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S2.p10.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a degree two map. Since this restriction map is defined by <math id="S2.p10.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔣</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 2.1. ‣ 2. The Hyperelliptic Factorization ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.<math id="S2.p10.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1)</annotation></semantics></math> guarantees that <math id="S2.p10.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔣</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=A</annotation></semantics></math>, which completes the proof of (a).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">To verify (b) and (c), write the hyperplane bundle <math id="S2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+n\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+n\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will show that <math id="S2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=g+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=g+2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔣</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(1)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(1)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, the exact sequence</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{C}\rightarrow 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{C}\rightarrow 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">induces the isomorphism</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<dl id="S2.I2" class="ltx_description">
<dt id="S2.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">  (2.1)</span></dt>
<dd class="ltx_item">
<div id="S2.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{i}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(n-j)\mathfrak{f}))\cong H^{i}(C,A^{g+2-j}\otimes B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{i}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(n-j)\mathfrak{f}))\cong H^{i}(C,A^{g+2-j}\otimes B)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></dd>
</dl>
</div>
<div id="S2.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p13.1" class="ltx_p">for <math id="S2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="S2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in{\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in{\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular,</p>
<table id="S2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(n-g-2)\mathfrak{f}))\cong H^{0}(C,B)\neq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(n-g-2)\mathfrak{f}))\cong H^{0}(C,B)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p13.2" class="ltx_p">while</p>
<table id="S2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(n-g-3)\mathfrak{f}))\cong H^{0}(C,A^{-1}\otimes B)=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(n-g-3)\mathfrak{f}))\cong H^{0}(C,A^{-1}\otimes B)=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p13.3" class="ltx_p">This implies that <math id="S2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=g+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=g+2</annotation></semantics></math>. Now we have</p>
<table id="S2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-g-2}=B." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{-g-2}=B.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p13.4" class="ltx_p">The value of <math id="S2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by using the degree of <math id="S2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed</p>
<table id="S2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{deg}(S)=g+3+b=(C_{0}+(g+2)\mathfrak{f})^{2}=-e+2(g+2)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>deg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{deg}(S)=g+3+b=(C_{0}+(g+2)\mathfrak{f})^{2}=-e+2(g+2)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p13.5" class="ltx_p">which shows that <math id="S2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=g+1-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=g+1-b</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, we determine the value of <math id="S2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> from the equality
<math id="S2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{deg}(\mathcal{L})=(C_{0}+(g+2)\mathfrak{f}).(2C_{0}+\ell\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>deg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{deg}(\mathcal{L})=(C_{0}+(g+2)\mathfrak{f}).(2C_{0}+\ell\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math>, where</p>
<table id="S2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{deg}(\mathcal{L})=2g+4+b\quad\mbox{and}\quad(C_{0}+(g+2)\mathfrak{f}).(2C_{0}+\ell\mathfrak{f})=-2e+\ell+2(g+2)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>deg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{deg}(\mathcal{L})=2g+4+b\quad\mbox{and}\quad(C_{0}+(g+2)\mathfrak{f}).(2C_{0}+\ell\mathfrak{f})=-2e+\ell+2(g+2).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.p13.6" class="ltx_p">Then we have <math id="S2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=b+2e=2g+2-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=b+2e=2g+2-b</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3. </span>Base Point Freeness And Very Ampleness</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this section we keep the previously introduced notation. In particular, <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a hyperelliptic curve of arithmetic genus <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The main purpose of this section is to prove</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a line bundle on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> with the factorization type <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each </span><math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{i}(C,\mathcal{L})=h^{i}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m))+h^{i}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m+b-g-1))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{i}(C,\mathcal{L})=h^{i}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m))+h^{i}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m+b-g-1)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, </span><math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is non-special if and only if </span><math id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+b\geq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+b\geq g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is base point free if and only if either</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.I1.ix2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I1.ix2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">a.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and hence </span><math id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\mathcal{L}}=\mathcal{O}_{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\mathcal{L}}=\mathcal{O}_{C})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> or</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">b.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq b\leq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq b\leq g+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+b\geq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+b\geq g+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is very ample if and only if either</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.I1.ix3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I1.ix3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">a.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and hence </span><math id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\mathcal{L}}=\mathcal{O}_{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\mathcal{L}}=\mathcal{O}_{C})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq g+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> or</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">b.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and hence </span><math id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\mathcal{L}}=\mathcal{O}_{C}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\mathcal{L}}=\mathcal{O}_{C}(P)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for some </span><math id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in C)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> or</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">c.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq b\leq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq b\leq g+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+b\geq g+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+b\geq g+2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I1.ix3.I2.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> be the rational ruled surface <math id="S3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b-g-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b-g-1))</annotation></semantics></math> with the minimal section <math id="S3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and a ruling <math id="S3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. By Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2. The Hyperelliptic Factorization ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>, <math id="S3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> as a divisor linearly equivalent to <math id="S3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2C_{0}+(2g+2-b)\mathfrak{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2C_{0}+(2g+2-b)\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, <math id="S3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔣</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, <math id="S3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the restriction of the line bundle <math id="S3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">(1) By (2.1), we have</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{CD}h^{i}(C,\mathcal{L})&amp;\quad=\quad&amp;h^{i}(C,A^{m}\otimes b)\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\\
&amp;\quad=\quad&amp;h^{i}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f}))\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\\
&amp;\quad=\quad&amp;h^{i}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m))+h^{i}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m+b-g-1))\end{CD}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>=</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:14em;" width="14em"></mspace></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>=</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:12em;" width="12em"></mspace></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>=</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{CD}h^{i}(C,\mathcal{L})&amp;\quad=\quad&amp;h^{i}(C,A^{m}\otimes b)\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\\
&amp;\quad=\quad&amp;h^{i}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f}))\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\\
&amp;\quad=\quad&amp;h^{i}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m))+h^{i}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m+b-g-1))\end{CD}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">(2) Remember that <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq b\leq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq b\leq g+1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=0</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="S3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is base point free if and only if <math id="S3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now assume that <math id="S3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})\cong H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})\cong H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f}))</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{Bs}~|\mathcal{L}|=C\cap\mbox{Bs}~|\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Bs</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mtext>Bs</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{Bs}~|\mathcal{L}|=C\cap\mbox{Bs}~|\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m&lt;g+1-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m&lt;g+1-b</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}\subset\mbox{Bs}~|\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mtext>Bs</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}\subset\mbox{Bs}~|\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})|</annotation></semantics></math> and hence <math id="S3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\cap C_{0}\subset\mbox{Bs}~|\mathcal{L}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mtext>Bs</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\cap C_{0}\subset\mbox{Bs}~|\mathcal{L}|</annotation></semantics></math>. This shows that <math id="S3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> fails to be base point free since <math id="S3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{length}~(C\cap C_{0})=b\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>length</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{length}~(C\cap C_{0})=b\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S3.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq g+1-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq g+1-b</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{Bs}~|\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})|=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Bs</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{Bs}~|\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})|=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> and so <math id="S3.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is base point free.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">(3) We need to classify all very ample line bundles among base point free line bundles. For <math id="S3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq g+2-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq g+2-b</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math> is a very ample line bundle on <math id="S3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, and so <math id="S3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is a very ample line bundle on <math id="S3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now assume that <math id="S3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq g+1-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq g+1-b</annotation></semantics></math>. By <math id="S3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is a base point free line bundle if and only if either</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S3.I2.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S3.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I2.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq m\leq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq m\leq g+1</annotation></semantics></math> or else</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S3.I2.ix2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S3.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I2.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq b\leq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq b\leq g+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.I2.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=g+1-b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=g+1-b</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Clearly <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is very ample if and only if <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq g+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Also for the case <math id="S3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>, the line bundle <math id="S3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(g+1-b)\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(g+1-b)\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math> is base point free, and defines an embedding of <math id="S3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\setminus C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\setminus C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore <math id="S3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> maps to a point. Observe that <math id="S3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{length}~(C\cap C_{0})=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>length</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{length}~(C\cap C_{0})=b</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f}))\cong H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f}))\cong H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can conclude that <math id="S3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is very ample if and only if <math id="S3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which completes the proof of (3).
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3.2</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\mbox{Pic}C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Pic</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\mbox{Pic}C</annotation></semantics></math> be a normalized line bundle of degree <math id="S3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(C,B)=\begin{cases}1&amp;\mbox{for $0\leq b\leq g$, and}\\
2&amp;\mbox{for $b=g+1$}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">, and</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(C,B)=\begin{cases}1&amp;\mbox{for $0\leq b\leq g$, and}\\
2&amp;\mbox{for $b=g+1$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Base Point Freeness And Very Ampleness ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.(1), <math id="S3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(C,B)=1+h^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b-g-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(C,B)=1+h^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b-g-1))</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary 3.3</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a base point free ample line bundle on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> with the hyperelliptic factorization type <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> fails to be very ample if and only if</span></p>
<ol id="S3.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(<math id="S3.I3.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for some </span><math id="S3.I3.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq m\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq m\leq g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(<math id="S3.I3.ix2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq b\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq b\leq g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="S3.I3.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and hence </span><math id="S3.I3.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(C,b)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(C,b)=1</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S3.I3.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext=")" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I3.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+b=g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+b=g+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">;</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I3.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(<math id="S3.I3.ix3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> 
<div id="S3.I3.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I3.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.I3.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a normalized line bundle of degree </span><math id="S3.I3.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I3.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">The assertion comes immediately by Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Base Point Freeness And Very Ampleness ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.(2) and (3).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">We conclude this section by investigating the maps of <math id="S3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> to projective spaces defined by <math id="S3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> in Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Corollary 3.3. ‣ 3. Base Point Freeness And Very Ampleness ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.(<math id="S3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>) <math id="S3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>). We obtain the following</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.4</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a base point free ample line bundle on <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, defining a morphism <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=h^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=h^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S3.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I4.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S3.I4.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S3.I4.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for some </span><math id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq m\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq m\leq g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> consists of the double covering </span><math id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> followed by the </span><math id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-uple embedding of </span><math id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> in </span><math id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. In particular, the image </span><math id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}(C)\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}(C)\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a rational normal curve of degree </span><math id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S3.I4.ix2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S3.I4.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume that </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq b\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq b\leq g</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and hence </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{0}(C,b)=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{0}(C,b)=1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(\mathcal{L})+b(\mathcal{L})=g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(\mathcal{L})+b(\mathcal{L})=g+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.
Let </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1}+\cdots+P_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1}+\cdots+P_{b}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> be the unique divisor in </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|b|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|b|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Then </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is nonspecial and the morphism </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{d-g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{d-g}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=\mbox{deg}(\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">deg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=\mbox{deg}(\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, is birational onto its image. More precisely, </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> maps </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> to a point </span><math id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in{\mathbb{P}}^{d-g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in{\mathbb{P}}^{d-g}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the restriction map</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}\upharpoonright_{C\setminus\{P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}\}}:C\setminus\{P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}\}\rightarrow\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}(C)\setminus\{q\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><msub><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↾</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}\upharpoonright_{C\setminus\{P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}\}}:C\setminus\{P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}\}\rightarrow\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}(C)\setminus\{q\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.ix2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is an isomorphism.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I4.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S3.I4.ix3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S3.I4.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a normalized line bundle of degree </span><math id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and the map </span><math id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a </span><math id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g+1)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.I4.ix3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-fold covering.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>, note that <math id="S3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=f^{*}\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=f^{*}\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m)</annotation></semantics></math> and also <math id="S3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})=f^{*}H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})=f^{*}H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m))</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq g</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>, let us remind of the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Base Point Freeness And Very Ampleness ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.<math id="S3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3)</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed <math id="S3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction of the line bundle <math id="S3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(g+1-b)\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(g+1-b)\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, which is base point free and defines an embedding of <math id="S3.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\setminus C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\setminus C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore <math id="S3.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> maps to a point, say <math id="S3.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S3.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}^{-1}(q)=C\cap C_{0}=\{P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}^{-1}(q)=C\cap C_{0}=\{P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the desired isomorphism</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\setminus\{P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}\}\cong\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}(C)\setminus\{q\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\setminus\{P_{1},\cdots,P_{b}\}\cong\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}(C)\setminus\{q\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2. The Hyperelliptic Factorization ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> asserts that <math id="S3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\cong{\mathbb{P}}_{1}^{1}\times{\mathbb{P}}_{2}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\cong{\mathbb{P}}_{1}^{1}\times{\mathbb{P}}_{2}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> as a divisor linearly equivalent to <math id="S3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2C_{0}+(g+1)\mathfrak{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2C_{0}+(g+1)\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the morphism <math id="S3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{\mathcal{L}}:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction of the second projection map <math id="S3.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}_{2}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}_{2}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, it is a <math id="S3.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(g+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(g+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-fold covering.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4. </span>Minimal Free Resolution I - High Degree</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now wish to give a precise description of the minimal free resolution of a linearly normal hyperelliptic curve <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of arithmetic genus <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and of degree <math id="S4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 2g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2g+1</annotation></semantics></math>. The case where <math id="S4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq 2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq 2g</annotation></semantics></math> will be dealt with in the next section.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this section, let <math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a line bundle on <math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 2g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2g+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-special and very ample, and defines a linearly normal embedding</p>
<table id="S4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}={\mathbb{P}}^{r},\quad r=d-g." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}={\mathbb{P}}^{r},\quad r=d-g.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be the homogeneous coordinate ring of <math id="S4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be the vanishing ideal of <math id="S4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.
By a result in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx5" title="" class="ltx_ref">F</a>]</cite>, <math id="S4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is projectively normal and <math id="S4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-regular. Thus a minimal free resolution of <math id="S4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is of the form</p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow F_{r-1}\rightarrow\cdots\rightarrow F_{i}\rightarrow\cdots\rightarrow F_{1}\rightarrow I_{C}\rightarrow 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow F_{r-1}\rightarrow\cdots\rightarrow F_{i}\rightarrow\cdots\rightarrow F_{1}\rightarrow I_{C}\rightarrow 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}=R(-i-1)^{\beta_{i,1}}\oplus R(-i-2)^{\beta_{i,2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}=R(-i-1)^{\beta_{i,1}}\oplus R(-i-2)^{\beta_{i,2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our main result in this section is</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the situation just state, suppose that <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2g+1+p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2g+1+p</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(a)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1,1}={{r-1}\choose{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1,1}={{r-1}\choose{2}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(b)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1,2}=\cdots=\beta_{p,2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1,2}=\cdots=\beta_{p,2}=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,2}=(i-p){{r-1}\choose{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,2}=(i-p){{r-1}\choose{i}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for </span><math id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p+1\leq i\leq r-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p+1\leq i\leq r-1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(c)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i+1,1}=\beta_{i,2}-g{{r-1}\choose{i}}+(r-1){{r-1}\choose{i+1}}-{{r-1}\choose{i+2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i+1,1}=\beta_{i,2}-g{{r-1}\choose{i}}+(r-1){{r-1}\choose{i+1}}-{{r-1}\choose{i+2}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="S4.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq i\leq r-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq i\leq r-2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Therefore </span><math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfies property </span><math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> but fails to satisfy property </span><math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">(a) The assertion comes immediately from the <math id="S4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-normality of <math id="S4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">(b) Let <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sheaf of ideals of <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\Omega_{{\mathbb{P}}^{r}}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\Omega_{{\mathbb{P}}^{r}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.1)</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,2}=h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,2}=h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(2))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math> be the hyperelliptic factorization type of <math id="S4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2. The Hyperelliptic Factorization ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> shows that <math id="S4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in <math id="S4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S={\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b-g-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S={\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b-g-1))</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore,
for the minimal section <math id="S4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and a fiber <math id="S4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math> of the projection map <math id="S4.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following three conditions hold:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=A,\quad\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=B,\quad\mbox{and}\quad C\equiv 2C_{0}+(2g+2-b)\mathfrak{f}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔣</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mi>C</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=A,\quad\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=B,\quad\mbox{and}\quad C\equiv 2C_{0}+(2g+2-b)\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">In particular, <math id="S4.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the restriction of <math id="S4.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L:=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L:=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Remember that <math id="S4.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is a very ample line bundle on <math id="S4.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> except the following cases:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(<math id="S4.I3.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I3.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=0</annotation></semantics></math> (and hence <math id="S4.I3.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="S4.I3.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=g+1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I3.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(<math id="S4.I3.ix2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> 
<div id="S4.I3.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=1</annotation></semantics></math> (and hence <math id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\mathcal{O}_{C}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\mathcal{O}_{C}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in C</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="S4.I3.ix2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=g</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We first consider the case where <math id="S4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is very ample. Then the two exceptional cases (<math id="S4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>) and (<math id="S4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>) will be treated in turn.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose that <math id="S4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is a very ample line bundle on <math id="S4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. Then it defines a smooth rational normal surface scroll <math id="S4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sheaf of ideals of <math id="S4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider the short exact sequence</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I4.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.2)</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I4.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I4.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{S}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{C}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{S}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{C}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">This induces the cohomology long exact sequence</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I5.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.3)</span> 
<div id="S4.I5.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I5.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I5.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))\rightarrow H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))\rightarrow H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I5.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S4.I5.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I5.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I5.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})\rightarrow H^{2}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})\rightarrow H^{2}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S4.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction of <math id="S4.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. Also since <math id="S4.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-regular,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p15" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I6.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.4)</span> 
<div id="S4.I6.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I6.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I6.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))=H^{2}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))=H^{2}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.I6.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p16.1" class="ltx_p">Thus (4.1), (4.3) and (4.4) imply that</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p17" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I7" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I7.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.5)</span> 
<div id="S4.I7.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I7.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I7.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,2}=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,2}=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.I7.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="S4.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{S}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{S}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S4.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}=\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m)\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m+b-g-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}=\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m)\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(m+b-g-1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the kernel of the surjective homomorphism <math id="S4.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{E})\otimes{\mathbb{P}}^{1}\rightarrow\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{E})\otimes{\mathbb{P}}^{1}\rightarrow\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="S4.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}=\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-1)^{\oplus(r-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}=\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-1)^{\oplus(r-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Letting <math id="S4.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C_{0}+(m+b-g-1)\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C_{0}+(m+b-g-1)\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the following commutative diagram:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p19" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{CD}&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;0&amp;\\
&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\downarrow&amp;\\
&amp;0&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;M&amp;\\
&amp;\downarrow&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\downarrow&amp;\\
0\rightarrow&amp;\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}&amp;\rightarrow&amp;\pi^{*}H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{E})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}&amp;\rightarrow&amp;\pi^{*}\mathcal{E}&amp;\rightarrow 0\\
&amp;\downarrow&amp;&amp;\parallel&amp;&amp;\downarrow&amp;\\
0\rightarrow&amp;\mathcal{M}_{S}&amp;\rightarrow&amp;H^{0}(S,L)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}&amp;\rightarrow&amp;L&amp;\rightarrow 0\\
&amp;\downarrow&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\downarrow&amp;\\
&amp;M&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;0&amp;\\
&amp;\downarrow&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\\
&amp;0&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\\
\end{CD}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi>M</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>∥</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">→</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>L</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi>M</mi></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{CD}&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;0&amp;\\
&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\downarrow&amp;\\
&amp;0&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;M&amp;\\
&amp;\downarrow&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\downarrow&amp;\\
0\rightarrow&amp;\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}&amp;\rightarrow&amp;\pi^{*}H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{E})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}&amp;\rightarrow&amp;\pi^{*}\mathcal{E}&amp;\rightarrow 0\\
&amp;\downarrow&amp;&amp;\parallel&amp;&amp;\downarrow&amp;\\
0\rightarrow&amp;\mathcal{M}_{S}&amp;\rightarrow&amp;H^{0}(S,L)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}&amp;\rightarrow&amp;L&amp;\rightarrow 0\\
&amp;\downarrow&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\downarrow&amp;\\
&amp;M&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;0&amp;\\
&amp;\downarrow&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\\
&amp;0&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp;\\
\end{CD}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p20.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, the first column gives the short exact sequence</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p21" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I8" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I8.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.6)</span> 
<div id="S4.I8.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I8.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I8.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\bigwedge^{i}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\rightarrow\bigwedge^{i-1}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes M\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\bigwedge^{i}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\rightarrow\bigwedge^{i-1}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes M\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="S4.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, which induces the cohomology long exact sequence</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p23" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I9" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I9.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.7)</span> 
<div id="S4.I9.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I9.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I9.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdots\rightarrow H^{0}(S,\bigwedge^{i-1}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes M\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdots\rightarrow H^{0}(S,\bigwedge^{i-1}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes M\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I9.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S4.I9.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I9.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I9.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I9.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S4.I9.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I9.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I9.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I9.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S4.I9.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I9.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I9.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i-1}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes M\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})\rightarrow\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i-1}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes M\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})\rightarrow\cdots</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p24" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p24.1" class="ltx_p">Note that</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p25" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I10" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I10.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.8)</span> 
<div id="S4.I10.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I10.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I10.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{k}(S,\bigwedge^{i-1}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes M\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{k}(S,\bigwedge^{i-1}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes M\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.I10.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p26.1" class="ltx_p">since <math id="S4.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2}=\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C_{0}+3(m-g-1)\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2}=\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C_{0}+3(m-g-1)\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore (4.5), (4.7) and (4.8) show that</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p27" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I11" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I11.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.9)</span> 
<div id="S4.I11.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I11.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I11.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,2}~~=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.938em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,2}~~=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I11.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S4.I11.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I11.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I11.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}((2m+b-2g-2)\mathfrak{f}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}((2m+b-2g-2)\mathfrak{f}))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I11.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S4.I11.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I11.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I11.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(2m+b-2g-2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(2m+b-2g-2))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p28.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}=\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-1)^{\oplus(r-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}=\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-1)^{\oplus(r-1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m+b=2g+1+p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m+b=2g+1+p</annotation></semantics></math>, one can immediately check that <math id="S4.p28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,2}={{r-1}\choose{i}}h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(p-1-i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,2}={{r-1}\choose{i}}h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(p-1-i))</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof of (b) when <math id="S4.p28.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is a very ample line bundle on <math id="S4.p28.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we turn to the case <math id="S4.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S4.p29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=A^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=A^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S={\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-g-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S={\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-g-1))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p29.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(g+1)\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+(g+1)\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p29.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{g+2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{g+2}</annotation></semantics></math> be the map defined by <math id="S4.p29.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|L|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|L|</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.p29.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}=\psi(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}=\psi(S)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S4.p29.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a cone over a rational normal curve of degree <math id="S4.p29.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p29.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{S^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{S^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sheaf of ideals of <math id="S4.p29.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider the exact sequence</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p30" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I12" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I12.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.10)</span> 
<div id="S4.I12.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I12.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I12.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{S^{\prime}}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{C}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{C/S^{\prime}}\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{S^{\prime}}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{C}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{C/S^{\prime}}\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p31" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p31.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{S^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{S^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the restriction of <math id="S4.p31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.p31.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the same method as in (4.3) and (4.4), we have</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p32" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I13" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I13.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.11)</span> 
<div id="S4.I13.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I13.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I13.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,2}=h^{1}(S^{\prime},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S^{\prime}}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C/S^{\prime}}(2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,2}=h^{1}(S^{\prime},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S^{\prime}}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C/S^{\prime}}(2))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p33" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p33.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.p33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi\upharpoonright_{C}:C\rightarrow C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↾</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\upharpoonright_{C}:C\rightarrow C</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism, the exact sequence</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p34" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I14" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I14.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.12)</span> 
<div id="S4.I14.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I14.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I14.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{C/S^{\prime}}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S^{\prime}}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{C}\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{C/S^{\prime}}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S^{\prime}}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{C}\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p35" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p35.1" class="ltx_p">is the direct image of</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p36" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I15" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I15.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.13)</span> 
<div id="S4.I15.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I15.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I15.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{C}\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{S}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{C}\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p37" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p37.1" class="ltx_p">by <math id="S4.p37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:S\rightarrow S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:S\rightarrow S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, note that <math id="S4.p37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)=\mathcal{I}_{C/S^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{*}\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)=\mathcal{I}_{C/S^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p37.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> be the kernel of the evaluation map <math id="S4.p37.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(S,L)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}\rightarrow L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(S,L)\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}\rightarrow L</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.p37.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{S}=\psi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{S^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{S}=\psi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{S^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p38" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I16" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I16.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.14)</span> 
<div id="S4.I16.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I16.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I16.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(S^{\prime},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S^{\prime}}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C/S^{\prime}}(2))\cong H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(S^{\prime},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S^{\prime}}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C/S^{\prime}}(2))\cong H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p39" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p39.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore (4.11) and (4.14) imply that</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p40" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I17" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I17.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(4.15)</span> 
<div id="S4.I17.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I17.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I17.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,2}=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,2}=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.p41" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p41.1" class="ltx_p">Now one can compute <math id="S4.p41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,2}</annotation></semantics></math> by the formula in (4.9).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p42" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p42.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p42.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we consider the case <math id="S4.p42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="S4.p42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=A^{g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>g</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=A^{g}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}(P)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S4.p42.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P\in C</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.p42.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S={\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-g))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S={\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-g))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p42.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+g\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+g\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.p42.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi:S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi:S\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the map defined by <math id="S4.p42.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|L|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|L|</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.p42.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}=\psi(S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}=\psi(S)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S4.p42.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is a cone over a rational normal curve of degree <math id="S4.p42.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.p42.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi\upharpoonright_{C}:C\rightarrow C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↾</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\upharpoonright_{C}:C\rightarrow C</annotation></semantics></math> is an isomorphism, all the arguments in the proof of <math id="S4.p42.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> are available for this case, and so <math id="S4.p42.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,2}</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by the formula in (4.9).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p43" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p43.1" class="ltx_p">(c) The Hilbert series of the homogeneous coordinate ring <math id="S4.p43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{C}=R/I_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{C}=R/I_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.p43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{R_{C}}(\lambda)=\frac{g\lambda^{2}+(g+p)\lambda+1}{(1-\lambda)^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{R_{C}}(\lambda)=\frac{g\lambda^{2}+(g+p)\lambda+1}{(1-\lambda)^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p43.2" class="ltx_p">On the use of Betti numbers <math id="S4.p43.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> we also may write</p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{R_{C}}(\lambda)=\frac{1-\beta_{1,1}\lambda^{2}+\sum_{k\geq 2}\{(-1)^{k}\beta_{k,1}+(-1)^{k-1}\beta_{k-1,2}\}\lambda^{k+1}}{(1-\lambda)^{r+1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{R_{C}}(\lambda)=\frac{1-\beta_{1,1}\lambda^{2}+\sum_{k\geq 2}\{(-1)^{k}\beta_{k,1}+(-1)^{k-1}\beta_{k-1,2}\}\lambda^{k+1}}{(1-\lambda)^{r+1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p43.3" class="ltx_p">Then the formula in (c) is obtained by comparing the coefficients.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5. </span>Minimal Free Resolution II - Low Degree</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our next aim is to study the minimal free resolution of a linearly normal hyperelliptic curve <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of arithmetic genus <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and of degree <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq 2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq 2g</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a very ample line bundle on <math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq 2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq 2g</annotation></semantics></math> and with the hyperelliptic factorization type <math id="S5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Base Point Freeness And Very Ampleness ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> says that <math id="S5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq b\leq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq b\leq g+1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+b\geq g+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+b\geq g+2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-special. Now consider the linearly normal embedding</p>
<table id="S5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}={\mathbb{P}}^{r},\quad r=d-g." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}={\mathbb{P}}^{r},\quad r=d-g.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">of <math id="S5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> defined by <math id="S5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{L}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{L}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> be the homogeneous coordinate ring of <math id="S5.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S5.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be the vanishing ideal of <math id="S5.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{\bullet}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{\bullet}</annotation></semantics></math> be a minimal free resolution of <math id="S5.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="S5.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{F}}_{\bullet}:0\rightarrow F_{r}\rightarrow\cdots\rightarrow F_{i}\rightarrow\cdots\rightarrow F_{1}\rightarrow I_{C}\rightarrow 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mo>∙</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{F}}_{\bullet}:0\rightarrow F_{r}\rightarrow\cdots\rightarrow F_{i}\rightarrow\cdots\rightarrow F_{1}\rightarrow I_{C}\rightarrow 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}=\bigoplus_{j\in{\mathbb{Z}}}R(-i-j)^{\beta_{i,j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}=\bigoplus_{j\in{\mathbb{Z}}}R(-i-j)^{\beta_{i,j}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We first introduce to some notation:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5.1</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a very ample line bundle <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq 2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq 2g</annotation></semantics></math> with the hyperelliptic factorization type <math id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S5.I1.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S5.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu:=\lceil\frac{b-1}{m+b-g-1}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu:=\lceil\frac{b-1}{m+b-g-1}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S5.I1.ix2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S5.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau:=\lfloor\frac{2g+1-b}{m}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau:=\lfloor\frac{2g+1-b}{m}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S5.I1.ix3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S5.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p:=(m+b-g-1)\times\nu-b+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p:=(m+b-g-1)\times\nu-b+1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Clearly, one can read off the integer <math id="S5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> from the identity <math id="S5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=\frac{b-1+p}{m+b-g-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=\frac{b-1+p}{m+b-g-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> since we consider the case where <math id="S5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq 2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq 2g</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The following is our main result in this section:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the situation just stated, let</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all </span><math id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))=\sum_{k=0}^{j-2}h^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(k(g+1-b)+2g-b-jm))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))=\sum_{k=0}^{j-2}h^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(k(g+1-b)+2g-b-jm)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, </span><math id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is </span><math id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">-normal if and only if </span><math id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq\nu</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">. Therefore </span><math id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{reg}(C)=\nu+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">reg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{reg}(C)=\nu+1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The graded Betti numbers </span><math id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">’s are as follows:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.I2.ix2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I2.ix2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,1}=i{{r}\choose{i+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,1}=i{{r}\choose{i+1}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for all </span><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,j}=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> for </span><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq j\leq\tau-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq j\leq\tau-1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and all </span><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iii)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1,\nu}=\cdots=\beta_{p,\nu}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1,\nu}=\cdots=\beta_{p,\nu}=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> and </span><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p+1,\nu}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p+1,\nu}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iv)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iv)</annotation></semantics></math></span> 
<div id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{r,\nu}=2g+1-d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{r,\nu}=2g+1-d</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix2.I1.ix4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I2.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I2.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If </span><math id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> fails to satisfy property </span><math id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nu,1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nu,1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, and if </span><math id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">, then </span><math id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> satisfies property </span><math id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nu,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nu,p}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> while it fails to satisfy property </span><math id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nu,p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nu,p+1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.I2.ix3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S={\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b-g-1))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo>⊕</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S={\mathbb{P}}(\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}\oplus\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(b-g-1))</annotation></semantics></math> be the rational ruled surface constructed in Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ 2. The Hyperelliptic Factorization ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>. Recall the following conditions:</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=A,\quad\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=B,\quad\mbox{and}\quad C\equiv 2C_{0}+(2g+2-b)\mathfrak{f}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝔣</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mi>C</mi><mo>≡</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(\mathfrak{f})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=A,\quad\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0})\otimes\mathcal{O}_{C}=B,\quad\mbox{and}\quad C\equiv 2C_{0}+(2g+2-b)\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Also <math id="S5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to the restriction of the line bundle <math id="S5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L:=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L:=\mathcal{O}_{S}(C_{0}+m\mathfrak{f})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, a crucial fact is that <math id="S5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is very ample since <math id="S5.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m+b\geq g+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m+b\geq g+2</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="S5.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|L|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|L|</annotation></semantics></math> defines a smooth rational normal surface scroll <math id="S5.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> which contains <math id="S5.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Keeping these situation in mind, let us begin with the proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">(1) From (4.2), we can prove that</p>
<table id="S5.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))\cong H^{1}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})\quad\mbox{for all $j\geq 2$}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))\cong H^{1}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})\quad\mbox{for all $j\geq 2$}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\equiv 2C_{0}+(2g+2-b)\mathfrak{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\equiv 2C_{0}+(2g+2-b)\mathfrak{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get the desired formula</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S5.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I3.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))=h^{1}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))=h^{1}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I3.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S5.I3.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I3.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=h^{1}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}((j-2)C_{0}+(jm+b-2g-2)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=h^{1}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}((j-2)C_{0}+(jm+b-2g-2)))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I3.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S5.I3.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I3.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I3.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\sum_{k=0}^{j-2}h^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(k(g+1-b)+2g-b-jm))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\sum_{k=0}^{j-2}h^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(k(g+1-b)+2g-b-jm))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore <math id="S5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))=0</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(j-2)(g+1-b)+2g-b-jm\leq-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(j-2)(g+1-b)+2g-b-jm\leq-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">or equivalently <math id="S5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq\nu</annotation></semantics></math>. This implies that <math id="S5.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{reg}(C)=\nu+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>reg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{reg}(C)=\nu+1</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S5.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-special.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p10.1" class="ltx_p">(2) To prove <math id="S5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math>, we will first show that</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p11" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I4.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.2)</span> 
<div id="S5.I4.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I4.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I4.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))=H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))=H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.I4.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Indeed, in the exact sequence</p>
<table id="S5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))\rightarrow H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))\rightarrow H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})\rightarrow 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{S}(j))\rightarrow H^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))\rightarrow H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p12.2" class="ltx_p">induced by (4.2), the third term</p>
<table id="S5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})=H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}((j-2)C_{0}+(jm-2g-2+b)\mathfrak{f}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})=H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}((j-2)C_{0}+(jm-2g-2+b)\mathfrak{f}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p12.3" class="ltx_p">vanishes if and only if <math id="S5.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="jm-2g-2+b\leq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">jm-2g-2+b\leq-1</annotation></semantics></math>, or equivalently <math id="S5.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. Clearly (5.2) implies that for <math id="S5.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq\tau-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq\tau-1</annotation></semantics></math>,
the <math id="S5.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th row of the Betti diagram of <math id="S5.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with those of the Betti diagram of <math id="S5.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, which completes the proof of <math id="S5.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(ii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(ii)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iii)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iii)</annotation></semantics></math>, note that <math id="S5.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>-normal and hence</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p14" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I5.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.3)</span> 
<div id="S5.I5.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I5.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I5.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{i,\nu}=h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(\nu))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{i,\nu}=h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(\nu))</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.I5.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p15.1" class="ltx_p">Also since <math id="S5.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nu+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nu+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-regular, it satisfies property <math id="S5.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nu,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nu,p}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S5.p15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p,\nu}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p,\nu}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. By using the same method as in (4.3) and (4.4), we know that</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p16" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I6.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.4)</span> 
<div id="S5.I6.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I6.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I6.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p,\nu}=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{p}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>p</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p,\nu}=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{p}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p17.1" class="ltx_p">Then by (4.6), the vanishing of <math id="S5.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p,\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p,\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> is verified if</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p18" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I7" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I7.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.5)</span> 
<div id="S5.I7.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I7.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I7.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{p}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>p</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{p}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu})=0</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p19.1" class="ltx_p">and</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p20" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I8" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I8.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.6)</span> 
<div id="S5.I8.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I8.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I8.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{p-1}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes M\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{p-1}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes M\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p21.1" class="ltx_p">For (5.5), note that <math id="S5.p21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{p}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>p</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{p}\pi^{*}\mathcal{M}_{\mathcal{E}}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu})</annotation></semantics></math> is isomorphic to a direct sum of copies of cohomology groups of the form</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p22" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I9" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I9.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.7)</span> 
<div id="S5.I9.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I9.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I9.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(\nu m-p-(k+2)(g+1-b)-b))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(\nu m-p-(k+2)(g+1-b)-b))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p23" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p23.1" class="ltx_p">with <math id="S5.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq k\leq\nu-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq k\leq\nu-2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since</p>
<table id="S5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu m-p-(k+2)(g+1-b)-b\geq\nu m-p-\nu(g+1-b)-b=-1," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu m-p-(k+2)(g+1-b)-b\geq\nu m-p-\nu(g+1-b)-b=-1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p23.2" class="ltx_p">the cohomology group in (5.7) vanishes, which completes the proof of (5.5). By the same way, we can check (5.6), and so <math id="S5.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies property <math id="S5.p23.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nu,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nu,p}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now it remains to show that
property <math id="S5.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nu,p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nu,p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> fails to hold, or equivalently, <math id="S5.p24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p+1,\nu}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p+1,\nu}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. To this aim, we use the finite scheme <math id="S5.p24.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma=C\cap C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma=C\cap C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Remember that <math id="S5.p24.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{C}(\Gamma)=B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{C}(\Gamma)=B</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, we will show that <math id="S5.p24.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a geometric obstruction for property <math id="S5.p24.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nu,p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nu,p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.p24.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.p24.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.p24.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>-normal, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p25" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I10" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I10.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.8)</span> 
<div id="S5.I10.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I10.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I10.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p+1,\nu}=h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(\nu))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p+1,\nu}=h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(\nu))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p26" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p26.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sheaf of ideals of <math id="S5.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, and consider the exact sequence</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p27" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I11" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I11.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.9)</span> 
<div id="S5.I11.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I11.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I11.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{C}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}\rightarrow B^{-1}\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{C}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}\rightarrow B^{-1}\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p28" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p28.1" class="ltx_p">This induces the cohomology long exact sequence</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p29" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I12" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I12.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.10)</span> 
<div id="S5.I12.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I12.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I12.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(\nu))\rightarrow H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}(\nu))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(\nu))\rightarrow H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}(\nu))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I12.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S5.I12.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I12.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I12.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow H^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L}^{\nu}\otimes B^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow H^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L}^{\nu}\otimes B^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p30" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p30.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction of <math id="S5.p30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.p30.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. By (5.8) and (5.10), <math id="S5.p30.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p+1,\nu}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p+1,\nu}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> if the second term of (5.10) is nonzero while the third term is zero.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.p31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-regular as a coherent sheaf on <math id="S5.p31.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p31.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L}^{\nu-1})=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L}^{\nu-1})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p31.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p31.2.1" class="ltx_text">This implies that <math id="S5.p31.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L}^{\nu}\otimes B^{-1})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L}^{\nu}\otimes B^{-1})=0</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S5.p31.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\otimes B^{-1}=A^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\otimes B^{-1}=A^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is an effective divisor on <math id="S5.p31.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p32" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text">We turn to the proof of the non-vanishing of <math id="S5.p32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}(\nu))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}(\nu))</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.p32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda={\mathbb{P}}^{m+b-g-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda={\mathbb{P}}^{m+b-g-1}</annotation></semantics></math> be the linear span of <math id="S5.p32.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S5.p32.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}\subset\mathcal{O}_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}\subset\mathcal{O}_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sheaf of ideals of <math id="S5.p32.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\subset\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\subset\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S5.p32.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\Lambda/{\mathbb{P}}^{r}}\subset\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{r}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\Lambda/{\mathbb{P}}^{r}}\subset\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{r}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the sheaf of ideals of <math id="S5.p32.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then from the exact sequence <math id="S5.p32.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{\Lambda}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}\rightarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{\Lambda}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>, one can show that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(5.11)\quad\quad H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}(\nu))\cong H^{1}(\Lambda,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}^{\prime}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}(\nu))\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5.11</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mover><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(5.11)\quad\quad H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}(\nu))\cong H^{1}(\Lambda,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}^{\prime}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}(\nu))\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p32.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p32.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="S5.p32.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the restriction of <math id="S5.p32.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.p32.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S5.p32.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\Lambda}:=\Omega_{\Lambda}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\Lambda}:=\Omega_{\Lambda}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> is a direct summand of <math id="S5.p32.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(5.12)\quad\quad H^{1}(\Lambda,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{\Lambda}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}(\nu))\subset H^{1}(\Lambda,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}^{\prime}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}(\nu))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5.12</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mover><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(5.12)\quad\quad H^{1}(\Lambda,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{\Lambda}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}(\nu))\subset H^{1}(\Lambda,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}^{\prime}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}(\nu)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p32.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p32.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.p32.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{length}(\Gamma)=b=\nu(m+b-g-1)+1-p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>length</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{length}(\Gamma)=b=\nu(m+b-g-1)+1-p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p32.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the rational normal curve <math id="S5.p32.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}\subset\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}\subset\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5. Minimal Free Resolution II - Low Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> below says that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(\Lambda,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{\Lambda}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}(\nu))\neq 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(\Lambda,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{\Lambda}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}(\nu))\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p32.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p32.4.1" class="ltx_text">In conclusion, <math id="S5.p32.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p,\nu}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p,\nu}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and so <math id="S5.p32.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> fails to satisfy property <math id="S5.p32.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nu,p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nu,p+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p33" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="S5.p33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(iv)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(iv)</annotation></semantics></math>, note that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{r,\nu}=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{r}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mi>r</mi></mover><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{r,\nu}=h^{1}(S,\bigwedge^{r}\mathcal{M}_{S}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p33.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p33.2.1" class="ltx_text">by the same method as in (4.3) and (4.4). Since <math id="S5.p33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigwedge^{r}\mathcal{M}=L^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>r</mi></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigwedge^{r}\mathcal{M}=L^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{r,\nu}=h^{1}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu-1})=2g+1-d." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{r,\nu}=h^{1}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{\nu-1})=2g+1-d.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.p34" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p34.1" class="ltx_p">(3) The assertion comes directly from (2).
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5.3</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a rational normal curve of degree <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\subset Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\subset Y</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite subscheme of length <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=\nu n+t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=\nu n+t</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-n+2\leq t\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-n+2\leq t\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for the sheaf of ideals <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}:=\Omega_{{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}:=\Omega_{{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{n},\bigwedge^{2-t}\mathcal{M}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}(\nu))\neq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{n},\bigwedge^{2-t}\mathcal{M}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}(\nu))\neq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.p35" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p35.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p35.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S5.p35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the restriction of <math id="S5.p35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.p35.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>. Remember that <math id="S5.p35.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies property <math id="S5.p35.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.p35.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus the exact sequence</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{Y}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-\ell)\rightarrow 0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{Y}\rightarrow\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}\rightarrow\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-\ell)\rightarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p35.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p35.2.1" class="ltx_text">induces the isomorphisms</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p36" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I13" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I13.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.13)</span> 
<div id="S5.I13.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I13.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I13.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{n},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}(j))\cong H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{Y}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(nj-\ell))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{n},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/{\mathbb{P}}^{n}}(j))\cong H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{Y}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(nj-\ell))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p37" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p37.1" class="ltx_p">for all <math id="S5.p37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.p37.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{Y}=\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-1)^{\oplus n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>⊕</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{Y}=\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-1)^{\oplus n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p38" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I14" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I14.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.14)</span> 
<div id="S5.I14.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I14.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I14.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{Y}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(nj-\ell))={{n}\choose{i}}h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-i+nj-\ell))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mi>i</mi></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\bigwedge^{i}\mathcal{M}_{Y}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(nj-\ell))={{n}\choose{i}}h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-i+nj-\ell))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p39" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p39.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, for <math id="S5.p39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=2-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=2-t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=\nu</annotation></semantics></math> we have</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p40" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S5.I15" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S5.I15.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(5.15)</span> 
<div id="S5.I15.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I15.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I15.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\bigwedge^{2-t}\mathcal{M}_{Y}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(n\nu-\ell))={{n}\choose{2-t}}h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>Y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\bigwedge^{2-t}\mathcal{M}_{Y}\otimes\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(n\nu-\ell))={{n}\choose{2-t}}h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(-2))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I15.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S5.I15.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I15.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S5.I15.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="={{n}\choose{2-t}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">={{n}\choose{2-t}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S5.p41" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p41.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is completed by combining (5.13) and (5.15).
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6. </span>Minimal Free Resolution III - Geometric Meaning</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a hyperelliptic curve of arithmetic genus <math id="S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a very ample line bundle on <math id="S6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and with the factorization type <math id="S6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>. In the previous two sections, we study the minimal free resolution of the linearly normal curve</p>
<table id="S6.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}={\mathbb{P}}^{r},\quad r=d-g," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}={\mathbb{P}}^{r},\quad r=d-g,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">embedded by <math id="S6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{L}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{L}|</annotation></semantics></math>. This section will be devoted to explain some related geometric meaning of our results. We will deal with the case where <math id="S6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 2g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 2g+1</annotation></semantics></math> and the case where <math id="S6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq 2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq 2g</annotation></semantics></math> in turn. 
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6.1. High Degree</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2g+1+p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2g+1+p</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies property <math id="S6.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> while it fails to satisfy property <math id="S6.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also the graded Betti numbers are precisely determined by <math id="S6.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> (Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4. Minimal Free Resolution I - High Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>). In particular, they are independent on <math id="S6.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>, and so one cannot determine <math id="S6.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math> from the minimal free resolution. On the other hand, <math id="S6.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math> gives us the precise numerical type of the rational ruled surface scroll</p>
<table id="S6.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S^{\prime}=\bigcup_{y\in{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}&lt;f^{-1}(y)&gt;\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.111em">&lt;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}=\bigcup_{y\in{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}&lt;f^{-1}(y)&gt;\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:C\rightarrow{\mathbb{P}}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the double covering. And in Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4. Minimal Free Resolution I - High Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, the graded Betti numbers of <math id="S6.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> are calculated by using <math id="S6.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="S6.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a geometric obstruction of property <math id="S6.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we will show that the failure of property <math id="S6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> can be explained by a specific finite subscheme of <math id="S6.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S6.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=A^{m}\otimes B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=A^{m}\otimes B</annotation></semantics></math> be the hyperelliptic factorization of <math id="S6.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the followings are equivalent:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S6.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6.1)\quad\begin{cases}1.\quad H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes\omega_{C}^{-1})=H^{0}(C,A^{m-g+1}\otimes B)\neq 0\vskip 3.0pt plus 1.0pt minus 1.0pt\\
2.\quad\mbox{There exists a $(p+3)$-secant $(p+1)$-plane to $C$.}\\
3.\quad m\geq g-1\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>There exists a </mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>-secant </mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>-plane to </mtext><mi>C</mi><mtext>.</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6.1)\quad\begin{cases}1.\quad H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes\omega_{C}^{-1})=H^{0}(C,A^{m-g+1}\otimes B)\neq 0\vskip 3.0pt plus 1.0pt minus 1.0pt\\
2.\quad\mbox{There exists a $(p+3)$-secant $(p+1)$-plane to $C$.}\\
3.\quad m\geq g-1\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Let us recall Theorem 1.1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx4" title="" class="ltx_ref">EGHP</a>]</cite>, which asserts that if a non-degenerate closed subscheme <math id="S6.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a <math id="S6.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+3)</annotation></semantics></math>-secant <math id="S6.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-plane, then it fails to satisfy the condition <math id="S6.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{2,p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{2,p+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore if <math id="S6.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\geq g-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\geq g-1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> fails to satisfy property <math id="S6.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> because there is a <math id="S6.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+3)</annotation></semantics></math>-secant <math id="S6.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-plane to <math id="S6.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. More precisely, any effective divisor <math id="S6.p6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in|A^{m-g+1}\otimes B|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in|A^{m-g+1}\otimes B|</annotation></semantics></math> spans a <math id="S6.p6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+3)</annotation></semantics></math>-secant <math id="S6.p6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-plane to <math id="S6.p6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Geometrically, <math id="S6.p6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle D\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle D\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is the span of <math id="S6.p6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and general <math id="S6.p6.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m+1-g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m+1-g)</annotation></semantics></math> rulings of <math id="S6.p6.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p7.1" class="ltx_p">From now on, we focus on the case where <math id="S6.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\leq g-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\leq g-2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S6.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is normalized and <math id="S6.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-g+1&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-g+1&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S6.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes\omega_{C}^{-1})=H^{0}(C,A^{m-g+1}\otimes B)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L}\otimes\omega_{C}^{-1})=H^{0}(C,A^{m-g+1}\otimes B)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="S6.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> does not admit a <math id="S6.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+3)</annotation></semantics></math>-secant <math id="S6.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-plane by (6.1). Note that <math id="S6.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{\prime}=S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>S</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{\prime}=S</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth. Let <math id="S6.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the minimal section of <math id="S6.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>. The finite scheme <math id="S6.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma:=C\cap C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma:=C\cap C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is of length <math id="S6.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=(p+g-m)+(g+1-m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=(p+g-m)+(g+1-m)</annotation></semantics></math> and spans the linear space <math id="S6.p7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda:=\langle C_{0}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda:=\langle C_{0}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> of dimension <math id="S6.p7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+g-m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+g-m)</annotation></semantics></math>. That is,</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p8" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I1.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6.2)</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I1.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda=\langle\Gamma\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda=\langle\Gamma\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S6.I1.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(p+g-m)+(g+1-m)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(p+g-m)+(g+1-m)\}</annotation></semantics></math>-secant <math id="S6.I1.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+g-m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+g-m)</annotation></semantics></math>-plane to <math id="S6.I1.ix1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p9.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g+1-m\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g+1-m\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, and so <math id="S6.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> fails to satisfy property <math id="S6.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+g-m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+g-m}</annotation></semantics></math> by Theorem 1.1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx4" title="" class="ltx_ref">EGHP</a>]</cite>. Now we will see that <math id="S6.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is a geometric obstruction of property <math id="S6.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. A crucial fact is that <math id="S6.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is contained in the rational normal curve <math id="S6.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.1</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> obstructs property <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the cohomology long exact sequence (5.10) for <math id="S6.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=2</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p11" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I2.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6.3)</span> 
<div id="S6.I2.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I2.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(2))\rightarrow H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}(2))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(2))\rightarrow H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}(2))</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I2.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<div id="S6.I2.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I2.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I2.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow H^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow H^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{m})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S6.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-special and <math id="S6.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies property <math id="S6.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p13" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I3" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I3.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6.4)</span> 
<div id="S6.I3.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I3.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I3.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p,1}=h^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p,1}=h^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p14.1" class="ltx_p">Clearly this implies that</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p15" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I4" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I4.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6.5)</span> 
<div id="S6.I4.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I4.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I4.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{m})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{1}(C,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{C}\otimes\mathcal{L}\otimes A^{m})=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p16.1" class="ltx_p">To prove the non-vanishing of the middle term in (6.3), we apply Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5. Minimal Free Resolution II - Low Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> to <math id="S6.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="S6.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Gamma|=2(p+g-m)+(1-p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Gamma|=2(p+g-m)+(1-p)</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 5.3. ‣ 5. Minimal Free Resolution II - Low Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a> shows that</p>
<table id="S6.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6.6)\quad\quad H^{1}(\Lambda,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{\Lambda}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}(2))\neq 0\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6.6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:10em;" width="10em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6.6)\quad\quad H^{1}(\Lambda,\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}_{\Lambda}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}(2))\neq 0\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p16.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\Lambda}=\Omega_{\Lambda}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\Lambda}=\Omega_{\Lambda}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma/\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> is the sheaf of ideals of <math id="S6.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\subset\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\subset\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. By the same argument as in (5.11) and (5.12), one can show that (6.6) implies</p>
<table id="S6.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6.7)\quad\quad H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}(2))\neq 0.\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6.7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:11.167em;" width="11.167em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6.7)\quad\quad H^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{\Gamma}(2))\neq 0.\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p16.3" class="ltx_p">In conclusion, <math id="S6.p16.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{p+1,1}=h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(2))\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{p+1,1}=h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\bigwedge^{p+1}\mathcal{M}\otimes\mathcal{I}_{C}(2))\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> by (6.3), (6.5) and (6.7), and hence <math id="S6.p16.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> fails to satisfy property <math id="S6.p16.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 6.2</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a smooth projective curve of genus <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a line bundle on <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2g+1+p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2g+1+p</annotation></semantics></math>. Theorem 2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx8" title="" class="ltx_ref">GL2</a>]</cite> says that <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math> fails to satisfy property <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if either <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a hyperelliptic curve or <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> admits a <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+3)</annotation></semantics></math>-secant <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p+1)</annotation></semantics></math>-plane. By our investigation in this subsection, every hyperelliptic curve <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> admit a finite subscheme <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma\subset C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma\subset C</annotation></semantics></math> which obstructs property <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{p+1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S6.Thmtheorem2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(C,\mathcal{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(C,\mathcal{L})</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6.2. Low Degree</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p18.1" class="ltx_p">Now we consider the case where <math id="S6.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is a very ample line bundle of degree <math id="S6.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq 2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq 2g</annotation></semantics></math> and with the factorization type <math id="S6.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5. Minimal Free Resolution II - Low Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> illustrates how <math id="S6.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math> effects on the shape of the minimal free resolution of <math id="S6.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r},~r=d-g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r},~r=d-g</annotation></semantics></math>. More precisely, the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity of <math id="S6.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to <math id="S6.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu+1</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S6.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=\frac{b-1+p}{m+b-g-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=\frac{b-1+p}{m+b-g-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also <math id="S6.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the condition <math id="S6.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nu,p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nu,p}</annotation></semantics></math> while it fails to satisfy the condition <math id="S6.p18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\nu,p+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\nu,p+1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus one can read off the values of <math id="S6.p18.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p18.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> from the minimal free resolution of <math id="S6.p18.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the identities</p>
<table id="S6.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6.8)\quad\quad d=2m+b\quad\mbox{and}\quad\nu=\frac{b-1+p}{m+b-g-1}\quad\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6.8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6.8)\quad\quad d=2m+b\quad\mbox{and}\quad\nu=\frac{b-1+p}{m+b-g-1}\quad\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p18.2" class="ltx_p">enables us to determine the pair <math id="S6.p18.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="S6.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6.9)\quad\quad m\quad=\quad d-g-1-\frac{2g+1+p-d}{\nu-2}\quad\quad\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6.9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mi>m</mi><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:3em;" width="3em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6.9)\quad\quad m\quad=\quad d-g-1-\frac{2g+1+p-d}{\nu-2}\quad\quad\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S6.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6.10)\quad\quad b\quad=\quad 2g+2-d+\frac{2(2g+1+p-d)}{\nu-2}\quad\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6.10</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mi>b</mi><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6.10)\quad\quad b\quad=\quad 2g+2-d+\frac{2(2g+1+p-d)}{\nu-2}\quad\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S6.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p19.1" class="ltx_p">Indeed, the factorization type interacts with the minimal free resolution more strongly in the following sense:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6.3</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be hyperelliptic curves of the same arithmetic genus <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be a very ample line bundles on <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\leq 2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\leq 2g</annotation></semantics></math> and with the factorization types <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{i},b_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{i},b_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C_{1},\mathcal{L}_{1})^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C_{1},\mathcal{L}_{1})^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C_{2},\mathcal{L}_{2})^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C_{2},\mathcal{L}_{2})^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> have the same graded Betti numbers if and only if <math id="S6.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m_{1},b_{1})=(m_{2},b_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m_{1},b_{1})=(m_{2},b_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S6.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.p20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\Longrightarrow)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Longrightarrow)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S6.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text"> Clear from (6.9) and (6.10).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p21" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p21.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.p21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\Longleftarrow)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟸</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Longleftarrow)</annotation></semantics></math> Let <math id="S6.p21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)=(m_{1},b_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)=(m_{1},b_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="S6.p21.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> be a line bundle with the factorization type <math id="S6.p21.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>. We keep the notations in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5. Minimal Free Resolution II - Low Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>. From (4.2), we have the following short exact sequence of <math id="S6.p21.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-modules:</p>
<table id="S6.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6.11)\quad\quad\quad 0\rightarrow I_{S}\rightarrow I_{C}\rightarrow E\rightarrow 0\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6.11</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:3em;" width="3em"></mspace><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:8em;" width="8em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6.11)\quad\quad\quad 0\rightarrow I_{S}\rightarrow I_{C}\rightarrow E\rightarrow 0\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p21.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S6.p21.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E:=\bigoplus_{j\in{\mathbb{Z}}}H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⨁</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E:=\bigoplus_{j\in{\mathbb{Z}}}H^{0}(S,\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)\otimes L^{j})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then (6.11) induces the following long exact sequence:</p>
<table id="S6.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(6.12)\cdots\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{S},K)_{i+j}\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{C},K)_{i+j}\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(E,K)_{i+j}\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6.12</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mtext>Tor</mtext><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mtext>Tor</mtext><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mtext>Tor</mtext><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mspace style="width:6em;" width="6em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6.12)\cdots\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{S},K)_{i+j}\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{C},K)_{i+j}\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(E,K)_{i+j}\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S6.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S6.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\quad\quad\quad\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i-1}^{R}(I_{S},K)_{i+j+1}\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i-1}^{R}(I_{C},K)_{i+j+1}\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i-1}^{R}(E,K)_{i+j+1}\rightarrow\cdots" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="3.278em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Tor</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Tor</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Tor</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\quad\quad\quad\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i-1}^{R}(I_{S},K)_{i+j+1}\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i-1}^{R}(I_{C},K)_{i+j+1}\rightarrow\mbox{Tor}_{i-1}^{R}(E,K)_{i+j+1}\rightarrow\cdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S6.p21.3" class="ltx_p">By Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5. Minimal Free Resolution II - Low Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>.(2).(i) and (ii) or the proof of them,</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p22" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I5" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I5.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6.13)</span> 
<div id="S6.I5.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I5.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I5.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{S},K)_{i+1}\cong\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{C},K)_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Tor</mtext><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Tor</mtext><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{S},K)_{i+1}\cong\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{C},K)_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.I5.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.p23" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p23.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p23.1.1" class="ltx_text">Also since <math id="S6.p23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S6.p23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-regular, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p24" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I6.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6.14)</span> 
<div id="S6.I6.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I6.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I6.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{S},K)_{i+j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Tor</mtext><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{S},K)_{i+j}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.I6.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I6.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.p25" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now (6.12), (6.13) and (6.14) enable us to show that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p26" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I7" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I7.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(6.15)</span> 
<div id="S6.I7.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I7.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S6.I7.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{C},K)_{i+j}\cong\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(E,K)_{i+j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Tor</mtext><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≅</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>Tor</mtext><mi>i</mi><mi>R</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(I_{C},K)_{i+j}\cong\mbox{Tor}_{i}^{R}(E,K)_{i+j}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S6.I7.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.I7.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that for any <math id="S6.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> with the factorization type <math id="S6.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the same pair (<math id="S6.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p27.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p27.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)</annotation></semantics></math>) and the isomorphisms in (6.15). Since the <math id="S6.p27.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>-module <math id="S6.p27.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by (<math id="S6.p27.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p27.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.p27.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{S}(-C)</annotation></semantics></math>), (6.13) and (6.15) completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 6.4</span></span><span id="S6.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a given <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\{g+3,g+4,\cdots,2g\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\{g+3,g+4,\cdots,2g\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the possible factorization types <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math> of a very ample line bundle of degree <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> are as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S6.I8" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S6.I8.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S6.I8.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I8.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S6.I8.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2k</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.I8.ix1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(m,b)\in\{(k-i,2i)~|~g+2-k\leq i\leq\lfloor\frac{g+1}{2}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)\in\{(k-i,2i)~|~g+2-k\leq i\leq\lfloor\frac{g+1}{2}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, there are exactly <math id="S6.I8.ix1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-\lceil\frac{g+1}{2}\rceil)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-\lceil\frac{g+1}{2}\rceil)</annotation></semantics></math> distinct factorization types.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I8.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S6.I8.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I8.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S6.I8.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2k+1</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S6.I8.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(m,b)\in\{(k-i,2i+1)~|~g+1-k\leq i\leq\lfloor\frac{g}{2}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.330em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.497em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)\in\{(k-i,2i+1)~|~g+1-k\leq i\leq\lfloor\frac{g}{2}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, there are exactly <math id="S6.I8.ix2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-\lceil\frac{g}{2}\rceil)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-\lceil\frac{g}{2}\rceil)</annotation></semantics></math> distinct factorization types.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore Theorem <a href="#S6.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 6.3. ‣ 6. Minimal Free Resolution III - Geometric Meaning ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6.3</span></a> shows that there exist precisely <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-\lceil\frac{g+1}{2}\rceil)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-\lceil\frac{g+1}{2}\rceil)</annotation></semantics></math> distinct Betti diagrams of linearly normal hyperelliptic curves of arithmetic genus <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and of degree <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2k</annotation></semantics></math>, and precisely <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k-\lceil\frac{g}{2}\rceil)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k-\lceil\frac{g}{2}\rceil)</annotation></semantics></math> distinct Betti diagrams of linearly normal hyperelliptic curves of arithmetic genus <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and of degree <math id="S6.Thmtheorem4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2k+1</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7. </span>Examples</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we provide some examples which illustrate the results in the present paper. Let <math id="S7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> be a hyperelliptic curve of arithmetic genus <math id="S7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> a very ample line bundle on <math id="S7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and with the factorization type <math id="S7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 7.1</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=g+3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=g+3</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)=(1,g+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)=(1,g+1)</annotation></semantics></math> by Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1. ‣ 3. Base Point Freeness And Very Ampleness ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.<math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=g</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=g</annotation></semantics></math>. Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5. Minimal Free Resolution II - Low Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> shows that</p>
<table id="S7.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{3},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))=\begin{cases}(j-1)(g-j)&amp;\quad\mbox{for $1\leq j\leq g$, and}\\
0&amp;\quad\mbox{for all $j\geq g+1$}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mtext>, and</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{3},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))=\begin{cases}(j-1)(g-j)&amp;\quad\mbox{for $1\leq j\leq g$, and}\\
0&amp;\quad\mbox{for all $j\geq g+1$}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Also <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by forms of degree <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq g+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq g+1</annotation></semantics></math> while it fails to be generated by forms of degree <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq g</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{C})_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{C})_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{C})_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{C})_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(I_{C})_{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(I_{C})_{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=g</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 7.2</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=g+4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=g+4</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)=(2,g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)=(2,g)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=g-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=g-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Also</p>
<table id="S7.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S7.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{4},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))=\sum_{k=0}^{j-2}h^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(g-2j+k))\quad\mbox{for all}\quad j\geq 2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>for all</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{4},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))=\sum_{k=0}^{j-2}h^{0}({\mathbb{P}}^{1},\mathcal{O}_{{\mathbb{P}}^{1}}(g-2j+k))\quad\mbox{for all}\quad j\geq 2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The vanishing ideal <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by forms of degree <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq g</annotation></semantics></math> while it cannot be generated by forms of degree <math id="S7.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq g-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq g-1</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 7.3</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=2g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=2g</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{g},\mathcal{I}_{C}(2))=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>g</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{g},\mathcal{I}_{C}(2))=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)=(g-i,2i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)=(g-i,2i)</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\leq i\leq\frac{g+1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\leq i\leq\frac{g+1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=i-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=i-2</annotation></semantics></math> and hence property <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{3,i-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{3,i-2}</annotation></semantics></math> holds but property <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{3,i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{3,i-1}</annotation></semantics></math> fails to hold for <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>g</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}^{g}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, if <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)=(g-2,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)=(g-2,4)</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> should have quartic generators while if <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)=(g-i,2i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)=(g-i,2i)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\leq i\leq\frac{g+1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\leq i\leq\frac{g+1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S7.Thmtheorem3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by quadratic and cubic equations. ∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S7.Thmtheorem4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 7.4</span></span><span id="S7.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To illustrate how the algebraic properties of <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subset{\mathbb{P}}H^{0}(C,\mathcal{L})^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> vary depending on <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,b)</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the case where <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=10</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13\leq d\leq 20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13\leq d\leq 20</annotation></semantics></math>. The previous examples explain the cases <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=13,14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=13,14</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math>. For the remaining cases, we tabulate the information obtained by Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2. ‣ 5. Minimal Free Resolution II - Low Degree ‣ COMPLETE LINEAR SERIESON A HYPERELLIPTIC CURVE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>. See Table 1 below. To simplify notation, we denote <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{1}({\mathbb{P}}^{r},\mathcal{I}_{C}(j))</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="S7.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</p>
</div>
</div>
